  "description": "Watch now | Plus this week's rankings—from worst to first.",
  "body_html": "<p>This is Mid Week Movers! Where I rank YOUR favorite stocks from worst to first. I end up buying the top stock today. Also, if you watch the video and want to check out the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/only-10-stocks-made-the-cut?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok ETF, that is crushing the S&amp;P 500, click here.</a></p><p>Lets hop right into it! </p><p>Starting with the worst…</p><h4><strong>Roblox &amp; Webull </strong></h4><ul><li><p>Price action is trending below the 200 day moving average. Maybe it breaks above, but without any retests behind us, we have no idea if a new bull trend is forming yet or not. We won big with Roblox last year…but that ship has sailed. It is in down trend, don’t fight it. </p></li></ul><h4><strong>Sandisk</strong></h4><ul><li><p>No good entry point (SEPA). Sandisk on the monthly and weekly charts have been strait up, with no consolidation zones or fresh breakouts. This would need to consolidate, and form a new high for me to consider. Additionally, the price action on smaller timeframes (daily) is trending downwards. </p></li></ul><h4><strong>Brightspring Health Services</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Nearly the same story as SNDK, this is a stock we traded profitably before. Right now I have no idea where a top is at, or whether it is in or not. I would want a local consolidation, and a fresh breakout, to consider this stock. </p></li></ul><p>Now at this point, we have only charts that are trending up. Trend is friend. I am just seeking to quickly eliminate a few more stocks with some simple rules. Sometimes analysts get way too technical with fundamentals. All we care about is:</p><ol><li><p>Are the shareholders making more money? (EPS)</p></li><li><p>Is the company generating more cashflow?</p></li></ol><p>And it does not even need to necessarily be cash flow positive. We care about improvement, annually and quarterly. Here was a review of each of the companies Cashflow and EPS, on both annual and quarterly levels. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png\" width=\"737\" height=\"365\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:365,&quot;width&quot;:737,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:41012,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/207153685?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!-5G3!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5a518c37-9be4-42f4-8d6f-422012f15999_737x365.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>I don’t expect every stock to be “perfect”, but we can eliminate all of the stocks that are not improving in 3 or 4 of the brackets. </p><h4><strong>This eliminates RVMD, CHEF and MPLX. </strong></h4><p>Please also note, even though I rank a stock low, it could still go up. But I am looking for optimal conditions, with high probabilities of going up! I want the chart to be solid on every timeframe, the fundamentals to back it, and preferably, a strong narrative to act as a catalyst. </p><h4>DELL</h4><p>Another quick cut, is DELL. The tech sector has been getting hammered. Yes, I know it has “always recovered” but when? Where is the bottom? With companies like Microsoft in a strait nose dive, since July 2025, and price action still trending downwards, I have no idea where the bottom is at. Additionally, Tech sector has been showing the most consistent weakness. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png\" width=\"572\" height=\"434\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:434,&quot;width&quot;:572,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:34836,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/207153685?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Zr-g!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa8988438-b9f1-4090-84d0-2c82a2711be0_572x434.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Tech showing the most consistent weakness the last month, and today. </figcaption></figure></div><p></p><p>Now, we are down to the final 9… we can start getting into the nitty gritty since basic requirements are being met. The stocks remaining are:</p><p>FFIV - Software</p><p>SN - Electronics</p><p>XMTR - Technology Services</p><p>ETN - Producer Manufacturing</p><p>AFRM - Finance</p><p>WT - Investment Trust/Mutual Funds</p><p>WTTR - Oil &amp; Gas Production</p><p>WEAV - Technology Services</p><p>LAMR - Finance, Real Estate</p><p>Which of these has the least relative strength? Not Relative Strength Index, which is largely useless (besides multiple divergences); relative strength is how strong a stock is performing, relative to the S&amp;P 500 or other stocks. Obviously, we want to eliminate the weakest relative strength. A quick an easy way to measure this is the <a href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/script/Z91eWlON-StockTok-Rocket-1-0/\">Indicator I built, free for you to use</a>, that measures relative strength (RS). </p><p><strong>Lets ditch 3 of these stocks, because they have the weakest relative strength: </strong></p><h4><strong>WT (66), LAMR (64) and ETN (62) ranked the lowest of the remaining stocks. </strong></h4><p><strong>Please do not forget to ❤️ and re-stack this post if you like it! Its how we beat out the AI slop on here. Thank you!</strong></p><h4><strong>We are down to the final 5! The top stock that I am buying is ⬇️</strong></h4>",
